From: CloudAndX <cloudandx@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] use TCG address translation when KVM is unavailable

Linux alone does not imply that the selected x86 guest accelerator was built
on an x86 host. Register the real KVM GPA translator only for Linux x86 host
builds; otherwise use the existing TCG physical-memory translator.

diff --git a/android-qemu2-glue/qemu-vm-operations-impl.cpp b/android-qemu2-glue/qemu-vm-operations-impl.cpp
--- a/android-qemu2-glue/qemu-vm-operations-impl.cpp
+++ b/android-qemu2-glue/qemu-vm-operations-impl.cpp
@@ -967,7 +967,7 @@ static void set_snapshot_callbacks(void* opaque,
                 set_address_translation_funcs(aehd_hva2gpa, aehd_gpa2hva);
                 break;
             case android::CPU_ACCELERATOR_KVM:
-#ifdef __linux__
+#if defined(__linux__) && (defined(__i386__) || defined(__x86_64__))
                 set_address_translation_funcs(0, kvm_gpa2hva);
 #else
                 set_address_translation_funcs(0, tcg_gpa2hva);
